# DIFO 2023 – Lab 2: Advanced Digital & Mobile Forensics

This lab focuses on advanced forensic analysis involving Android devices, application artifacts, and disk-level investigations.

---

## 🎯 Objectives
- Analyze Android file systems and partitions
- Extract and interpret application data
- Compare logical vs physical acquisition methods
- Perform disk forensic analysis
- Evaluate forensic soundness of acquisition methods

---

## 🛠️ Tools & Techniques
- Android Debug Bridge (ADB)
- SQLite database analysis
- Sleuth Kit (mmls, fls)
- Hash verification tools
- ssdeep (fuzzy hashing)
- Scalpel (file carving)
- Timeline reconstruction

---

## 🔍 Key Tasks Performed
- Identified Android app data locations
- Extracted email and browser artifacts
- Analyzed SQLite databases
- Recovered credentials from system files
- Performed disk partition analysis
- Carved Master File Table (MFT) entries
- Verified forensic integrity using hashes

